{\xe \v intel-ipsec-mb.h\:IMB_JOB}
\pard\plain \s4\sb240\sa60\keepn\widctlpar\adjustright \b\f1\fs20\cgrid {
{\b 
typedef struct IMB_JOB IMB_JOB}}
\par
{\bkmkstart AAAAAAAAJK}
{\bkmkend AAAAAAAAJK}
{
\pard\plain \s61\li360\sa60\sb30\qj\widctlpar\qj\adjustright \fs20\cgrid 
{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
Job structure.\par
For AES, enc_keys and dec_keys are expected to point to expanded keys structure.{
\par
\pard\plain {\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af0\langfe2052\dbch\af0\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af3\dbch\af3\loch\f8 \'01\u9702\tab}\ilvl1\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-360\tx720\li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-360\kerning1\hich\af4\dbch\af5\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs20
AES-CTR, AES-ECB and AES-CCM, only enc_keys is used\par
\pard\plain {\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af0\langfe2052\dbch\af0\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af3\dbch\af3\loch\f8 \'01\u9702\tab}\ilvl1\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-360\tx720\li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-360\kerning1\hich\af4\dbch\af5\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs20
DOCSIS (AES-CBC + AES-CFB), both pointers are used enc_keys has to be set always for the partial block\par}
For AES-GCM, AES-GCM-SGL and SM4-GCM, enc_keys and dec_keys are expected to point to the same key structure.{
\par
\pard\plain {\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af0\langfe2052\dbch\af0\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af3\dbch\af3\loch\f8 \'01\u9702\tab}\ilvl1\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-360\tx720\li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-360\kerning1\hich\af4\dbch\af5\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs20
enc_keys is used for encrypt direction and dec_keys for decrypt direction\par}
For DES, enc_keys and dec_keys are expected to point to DES key schedule.{
\par
\pard\plain {\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af0\langfe2052\dbch\af0\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af3\dbch\af3\loch\f8 \'01\u9702\tab}\ilvl1\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-360\tx720\li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-360\kerning1\hich\af4\dbch\af5\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs20
same key schedule used for enc and dec operations\par}
For 3DES, enc_keys and dec_keys are expected to point to an array of 3 pointers for the corresponding 3 key schedules.{
\par
\pard\plain {\*\hyphen2\hyphlead2\hyphtrail2\hyphmax0}\nowidctlpar\cf0\hich\af0\langfe2052\dbch\af0\afs24\lang1081\loch\f0\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \hich\af3\dbch\af3\loch\f8 \'01\u9702\tab}\ilvl1\ls1 \li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\fi-360\tx720\li720\ri0\lin720\rin0\fi-360\kerning1\hich\af4\dbch\af5\rtlch \ltrch\loch\fs20
same key schedule used for enc and dec operations\par}
Cipher offset only applies to src pointer, not dst pointer. In case of an in-place operation, dst pointer needs to point at src + cipher_start_src_offset_in_bytes. \par
}}
